PART II. UPGRADING AN EXISTING NODE
================================================================================

12. RULES AND PRE-UPGRADE CHECKS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- Do not run create_sysop.pl: it is NOT an upgrade step.
- Do not overwrite Listeners.pm or DXVars.pm without backup and review.
- DXVars.pm requires the controlled migration in section 15.
- Do not delete local/, local_data/, local_cmd/ or connect/.
- Do not use git reset --hard, git clean or git push.
- Do not modify or replace an existing service without reviewing it.
- If there are errors or unidentified local changes, STOP.

12.1 IDENTIFYING THE INSTALLATION AND SERVICE

As sysop, in a Linux terminal:

   sudo -iu sysop
   id -un
   cd /spider
   pwd -P
   git rev-parse --show-toplevel
   git branch --show-current
   git status --short
   git log -1 --oneline
   ls -l local/DXVars.pm local/Listeners.pm

Verify that the real directory and branch are as expected.
This guide uses the mojo branch. If there are local changes,
do not proceed until their purpose is understood.

In another terminal, as administrator, check the service:

   sudo systemctl status dxspider.service
   sudo systemctl cat dxspider.service

If systemd is unavailable or the service has a different name,
identify the actual startup method. Do NOT create another service in
parallel. Record the service name and how to stop it.


13. BACKUP AND SHUTDOWN
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The backup must include configuration, persistent data, connection scripts,
local commands and the current code revision. Do not
keep the only backup inside the tree being upgraded.

As sysop, from /spider, record the previous commit:

   cd /spider
   git rev-parse HEAD
   git status --short

Save that hash to identify the previous version.

As administrator, prepare a backup location outside the tree:

   sudo mkdir -p /var/backups/dxspider

IMPORTANT: a consistent data backup must be taken with
DXSpider stopped, especially when SQLite is in use.

13.1 STOPPING THE NODE AND COMPLETING THE BACKUP

If dxspider.service is used, as administrator:

   sudo systemctl stop dxspider.service
   sudo systemctl is-active dxspider.service

The expected result is 'inactive'. If it is still active, stop.
If the node was started manually, stop it using the usual
procedure and check that no other cluster.pl is running.

With the node stopped, as administrator:

   BACKUP="/var/backups/dxspider/dxspider-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S).tgz"
   test ! -e "$BACKUP" || exit 1
   sudo tar -C /home/sysop -czf "$BACKUP" spider
   sudo tar -tzf "$BACKUP" >/dev/null
   echo "$BACKUP"

Record the displayed path and keep it for a possible restore.

The backup contains private information. Protect it and check free
space before creating it. If the backup fails, do NOT
upgrade. The path /home/sysop/spider is valid only if verified in section 12.1.
If the installation is elsewhere, adjust -C and the tree name.


14. UPDATING THE MOJO BRANCH WITH GIT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

14.1 Stop DXSpider using the usual system procedure.

  Back up the installation and its data.

14.2 As SYSOP (from a user with sudo privileges)

   sudo -iu sysop
   id -un
   cd /ACTUAL/PATH/TO/SPIDER
   pwd -P
   git rev-parse --show-toplevel
   git status --short

  Replace /RUTA/REAL/DE/SPIDER with the actual existing path. Usually
  this is /home/sysop/spider. The operating owner
  in this guide is always sysop. If there are
  local changes, STOP and review them before proceeding.
  Do not run git reset --hard or git clean.

14.3 As SYSOP, and only with a clean working tree:

   git fetch git://scm.dxcluster.org/spider \
     +refs/heads/mojo:refs/remotes/dirk/mojo
   git show-ref --verify refs/remotes/dirk/mojo
   if git show-ref --verify --quiet refs/heads/mojo; then
     git switch mojo
   else
     git switch --create mojo --no-track refs/remotes/dirk/mojo
   fi
   git merge --ff-only refs/remotes/dirk/mojo

  If Git rejects the switch or update, STOP.
  Do not force merges or discard changes.

14.4 As SYSOP, verify:

   test "$(git branch --show-current)" = mojo
   test "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" = \
     "$(git rev-parse refs/remotes/dirk/mojo)"
   git status --short
   git log -1 --oneline

  Both hashes must match and the working tree must be clean.
  Exit using exit and restart DXSpider using the usual method.


15. VERSION REQUIREMENTS AND STARTUP
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

15.1 MIGRATING DXVars.pm DURING UPGRADES

The current version may require entries missing from an
old DXVars.pm. With DXSpider stopped and after backing up as
described in section 13, refresh the template and restore
the node-specific configuration. Do not copy another SYSOP configuration.

As sysop, from /spider, first check the files:

   cd /spider
   test -f local/DXVars.pm || exit 1
   test -f perl/DXVars.pm.issue || exit 1
   test ! -e local/DXVars.pm.old || {
     echo 'DXVars.pm.old already exists: STOP'; exit 1;
   }


15.1.1 Back up the current local file as DXVars.pm.old:

   cp -p local/DXVars.pm local/DXVars.pm.old

15.1.2 Copy the current version template to local/DXVars.pm:

   cp perl/DXVars.pm.issue local/DXVars.pm

15.1.3 Restore the previous configuration

  Edit the new local/DXVars.pm and transfer the
  node-specific values field by field from local/DXVars.pm.old:

   nano local/DXVars.pm

  View the old file in another terminal or with:

   less local/DXVars.pm.old

  Keep new variables and their default values where appropriate.
  Restore callsigns, QTH, locator, email, paths, options and any
  necessary custom settings from the old file. Do not replace
  the entire new file with the old copy.

15.1.4 Before starting, compare and review the configuration:

   diff -u local/DXVars.pm.old local/DXVars.pm

  Review new and customized variables especially carefully. If anything
  is unclear or incorrect, do NOT start until resolved. Keep
  DXVars.pm.old as a backup. Perform the migration once per
  upgrade that requires new entries; if already completed, do not
  repeat it or overwrite the backup.

15.2 VERIFYING REQUIREMENTS

Before startup, read the changes and instructions included
with the installed revision, especially UPGRADE.mojo, README_DXReg and
README_DXWeb.
Do not
assume that a code upgrade never changes requirements.

For upgrades, Git and iproute2 (which provides the ss command) must also
be available. Check before following the instructions:

   command -v git && command -v ss

If they are missing on Debian/Ubuntu/Raspberry Pi OS, as administrator:

   sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y git iproute2

On other distributions, review the appropriate package manager before installing
packages.

As sysop:

   cd /spider
   test -f UPGRADE.mojo && less UPGRADE.mojo
   test -f local/DXVars.pm || exit 1
   test -f local/Listeners.pm || exit 1

Review section 3 and check the required
modules. Install only missing dependencies using the appropriate package
manager. Controlled replacement of DXVars.pm is explained
above; preserve Listeners.pm and other local files. If
the new version requires a migration, follow its
specific instructions before starting. Do not improvise data conversions.

15.3 STARTING AND VERIFYING

If the node is managed by dxspider.service, as administrator:

   sudo systemctl start dxspider.service
   sudo systemctl --no-pager --full status dxspider.service
   sudo journalctl -u dxspider.service -n 80 --no-pager

If another startup method is used, continue using it.
Do not run perl/cluster.pl manually while the service is active.

From Linux, check that the configured port is listening:

   ss -ltn

Log in to the node as SYSOP and run these commands in the DXSpider console:

   sh/version
   sh/cluster
   sh/connect

Verify identity, version, SYSOP access, debug output and expected
connections. An 'active' process status alone does NOT prove that
the node is working correctly.


16. TROUBLESHOOTING AND FINAL CHECKS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Do not run create_sysop.pl, delete databases or repeat commands without
identifying the cause. Keep the logs and the previous Git hash.

As administrator, stop the affected service:

   sudo systemctl stop dxspider.service

Plan restoration according to the changes made, data
compatibility and the verified backup from section 13. Do
not blindly roll back Git: data migrations may have occurred.
If restoration is necessary, stop the service first
and verify the backup file contents and path.

16.1 FINAL CHECKLIST

[ ] Actual path, mojo branch and service identified.
[ ] Local changes reviewed before upgrading.
[ ] Previous commit recorded.
[ ] Node stopped and external backup verified.
[ ] Git updated as described in section 14.
[ ] Version instructions and dependencies reviewed.
[ ] DXVars.pm migrated and reviewed; .old retained.
[ ] Local Listeners.pm preserved.
[ ] Service started without errors.
[ ] SYSOP access, version, listener and debug output verified.
[ ] Network connections verified where applicable.

